<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" Class="mb-3">If you actually want to run it locally</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">Prerequisite: .NET 10 SDK.</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">From the repository root:</MudText>
<MudPaper Class="pa-3 mb-3" Elevation="0" Style="background-color: dimgrey; font-family: monospace; color: white;">
    dotnet run --project Library.Blazor
</MudPaper>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
    The repository ships with an already-migrated SQLite database
    (<code>Library.Blazor/Data/app.db</code>) and seeds the accounts above (plus the demo catalogue/loans/
    reservations/payments described above) automatically on first run against an empty database. If you delete
    that database file to start clean, apply the EF Core migrations before running again:
</MudText>
<MudPaper Class="pa-3 mt-2" Elevation="0" Style="background-color: dimgrey; font-family: monospace; color: white;">
    dotnet ef database update --project Library.Blazor
</MudPaper>
